(a) whether Government will provide district-wise details of implementation of Ayushman Bharat Pradhan Mantri Jan Arogya Yojana (AB-PMJAY) SEHAT, National Health Mission (NHM), PM-Ayushman Bharat Health Infrastructure Mission (PM-ABHIM), eSanjeevani, Mission Indradhanush and Nikshay in Jammu and Kashmir (J & K) during the last five years;
(b) the beneficiaries, hospitals upgraded, Health and Wellness Centres operational, funds allocated, released and utilised, district-wise;
(c) the districts with implementation delays and reasons therefor; and
(d) the corrective measures and timelines for universal healthcare coverage across all districts?

(a) the scheme-wise details of implementation of Regional Connectivity Scheme (RCS)-UDAN, UDAN 5.0, Krishi UDAN, Digi Yatra and airport infrastructure development projects in Jammu and Kashmir during the last three years;
(b) the district-wise status of Jammu, Srinagar, Udhampur and Kishtwar airport projects, including reasons for delays and revised completion timelines;
(c) the employment generated, directly and indirectly, through airports, airlines, ground handling, tourism and allied sectors; and
(d) whether new regional routes, heliports and aviation training facilities are proposed for Jammu and Kashmir to enhance connectivity, tourism and youth employment?

(a) funds allocated, released and utilised under Jal Jeevan Mission (JJM), Atal Bhujal Yojana, Jal Shakti Abhiyan: Catch the Rain, Namami Gange, National Hydrology Project and Pradhan Mantri Krishi Sinchayee Yojana (PMKSY) in Jammu and Kashmir during the last five years, district-wise details;
(b) contractor-wise pending payments, reasons for delays and timelines for clearance;
(c) details of reported irregularities, inspections and action taken; and
(d) district-wise uncovered habitations, water-scarce areas, pending projects and the completion schedule thereof?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the implementation of railway projects and passenger services in the Union Territory of Jammu and Kashmir during the last three years;
(b) the district-wise details of railway lines, stations, bridges, tunnels, electrification, signalling, passenger amenities and train services sanctioned, completed and under execution, along with the funds allocated, released and utilised;
(c) the reasons for delays, if any;
(d) the corrective measures taken and the timelines fixed for completion of all pending railway projects and connectivity initiatives; and
(e) the details of passenger and freight traffic generated?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the implementation of all schemes of Commerce and Industry in the Union Territory of Jammu and Kashmir during the last five years;
(b) the details of industrial units approved, investments received, employment generated, exports, startups recognised, GI product promotion, industrial estates developed, funds allocated, released and utilised and beneficiaries covered under various Central schemes, district-wise;
(c) the details of pending proposals and reasons therefor; and
(d) the corrective measures, monitoring mechanism and timelines fixed for completion of all pending projects and investment proposals?

(a) whether Government has implemented satellite-based applications and space technology programmes in the Union Territory of Jammu and Kashmir during the last five years;
(b) the district-wise details of projects undertaken through ISRO for disaster management, agriculture, horticulture, water resources, urban planning, border management and environmental monitoring;
(c) the year-wise details of funds sanctioned, released and utilised, along with beneficiary departments and implementing agencies; and
(d) whether Government proposes expanding satellite communication, remote sensing, geospatial services and capacity-building programmes in educational institutions and remote, border and tribal districts of Jammu and Kashmir?

(a) the district-wise details of funds sanctioned, released and utilised under Pradhan Mantri Janjatiya Unnat Gram Abhiyan (PMJUGA) and Dharti Aaba Janjatiya Gram Utkarsh Abhiyan (DAJGUA) in Jammu and Kashmir during the last three years;
(b) the district-wise list of panchayats and tribal villages covered, indicating allocations and works undertaken;
(c) the sector-wise convergence achieved in education, health, roads, drinking water, electricity, livelihoods, digital connectivity and other basic services; and
(d) the district-wise physical and financial progress, including the monitoring mechanism adopted to ensure timely implementation and effective utilisation of funds?

(a) district-wise details of funds sanctioned, released and utilised under Samagra Shiksha in the Union Territory of Jammu and Kashmir during each of the last three years;
(b) district-wise and component-wise details of works and interventions approved;
(c)  district-wise and school-wise details indicating the name of each school, UDISE Code, component-wise assistance, amounts sanctioned, released and utilised, physical progress and implementation status;
(d) the details of pending or delayed works, reasons therefor and expected completion dates; and
(e) the monitoring mechanism ensuring timely implementation and optimal fund utilisation?

bs

(a) whether Government has reviewed delays in implementing PM Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana, PM-KUSUM, Grid Connected Rooftop Solar Programme (Phase-II), National Green Hydrogen Mission, Bioenergy Programme and Small Hydro Power Programme in Jammu and Kashmir (J&K) during the last five years;
(b) the district-wise details of sanctioned, completed and delayed projects;
(c) the reasons for delays, including land, transmission, weather, funding and clearances; and
(d) the scheme-wise revised timelines, funds released, corrective measures, monitoring mechanisms, expected completion dates and anticipated benefits for consumers, farmers, institutions, industries and remote tribal areas across J&K?

(a) whether Government has reviewed implementation of the National Handloom Development Programme (NHDP), National Handicrafts Development Programme (NHDP), Silk Samagra-2, PM MITRA, SAMARTH, National Technical Textiles Mission and Integrated Wool Development Programme in the Union Territory of Jammu and Kashmir during the last five years;
(b) the details of funds allocated, released and utilised and the beneficiaries including weavers, artisans, sericulturists, wool growers, carpet weavers, Pashmina producers, women, Scheduled Tribes, Scheduled Castes, minorities, youth and self-help groups, district-wise;
(c) employment and exports generated; and
(d) pending projects with reasons therefor and corrective measures taken?

(a) whether Government is implementing schemes namely National Afforestation Programme (NAP), Green India Mission (GIM), Integrated Development of Wildlife Habitats (IDWH), Project Tiger, National Mission for Green India and Climate Change Action Programme (CCAP) in the Union Territory of Jammu and Kashmir;
(b) the scheme-wise funds allocated, released and expenditure incurred during the last five years;
(c) the district-wise details of works undertaken under each scheme;
(d) the number of employment opportunities generated and beneficiaries covered; and
(e) the details of implementing agencies and forest divisions involved in these programmes?

(a) whether the Central Sector Schemes (CSS) of the Ministry have been implemented in Jammu and Kashmir during the last five years;
(b) the scheme-wise details under Kala Sanskriti Vikas Yojana, National Mission on Libraries, National Mission for Manuscripts, Museum Grant Scheme and National Mission on Cultural Mapping;
(c) the year-wise funds allocated, released and utilized in the U.T.;
(d) the district-wise number of projects sanctioned, completed and ongoing; and
(e) the measures taken to safeguard tangible and intangible cultural heritage and promote artists in the U.T.?

(a) whether the National Livestock Mission (NLM) is being implemented in the Union Territory of Jammu and Kashmir;
(b) if so, the year-wise funds allocated, released and utilised under the Mission during the last five years;
(c) the district-wise details of beneficiaries supported for sheep, goat, poultry and piggery development under the scheme;
(d) the number of self-help groups, farmers and entrepreneurs assisted, district-wise; and
(e) whether Government proposes to expand the Mission to generate employment and improve livestock productivity across districts of Jammu and Kashmir?

(a) whether Government has implemented PM SVANidhi in Jammu and Kashmir and the number of street vendors identified and benefited thereunder;
(b) the total amount of collateral-free working capital loans sanctioned and disbursed so far under the scheme in the Union Territory;
(c) the details of business activities supported and whether the scheme has helped vendors flourish and become Atmanirbhar; and
(d) the Urban Local Body-wise and bank-wise details of beneficiaries and credit disbursed in Jammu and Kashmir?

(a) the block-wise details of works undertaken under the Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Act (MGNREGA) in Jammu & Kashmir during the last five years;
(b) the title and category of works approved, ongoing and completed in each block;
(c) the total number of works, person-days generated and expenditure incurred, year-wise and block-wise;
(d) the details of pending liabilities and delayed wage payments, if any; and
(e) steps taken to strengthen transparency, fund flow and implementation?

(a) whether various Central developmental schemes are being implemented in the Union Territory of Jammu and Kashmir to strengthen school and higher education sectors, including Samagra Shiksha, PM SHRI and PM USHA;
(b) the total funds allocated, released and utilized under these schemes during the last five financial years, along with district-wise details thereof; and
(c) the steps taken to address infrastructure gaps, teacher vacancies, digital connectivity challenges and monitoring mechanisms to ensure effective implementation across rural, tribal and border districts of the Union Territory?

(a) the details of centrally sponsored schemes implemented by the Ministry in the union territory of Jammu and Kashmir;
(b) the total funds allocated, released and utilized during the last three years, year-wise;
(c) the renewable energy capacity installed, source-wise;
(d) the number of beneficiaries under PM Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana, district-wise; and
(e) the steps taken to promote renewable energy in remote and border districts?

(a) whether, in view of the rapid growth of domestic aviation under Government’s airport modernisation initiatives, a time-bound plan has been formulated to progressively replace bus-based passenger transit at arrival and departure terminals with aerobridge-enabled boarding to reduce travel time and enhance passenger convenience;
(b) the airport-wise and State-wise details of existing aerobridges vis-à-vis total operational aircraft parking bays; and
(c) the projected expansion targets and timelines for installation of additional aerobridges across major and regional airports?

(a) whether, in furtherance of Government’s efforts to strengthen connectivity and promote development in the Union Territories of Jammu and Kashmir and Ladakh, proposals have been examined for establishing new airports or civil enclaves in districts distant from Jammu and Srinagar airports, particularly Rajouri, Poonch and Kishtwar;
(b) whether feasibility studies or land identification have been undertaken in these districts and in Kargil;
(c) whether civilian use of existing defence airstrips in these areas has been considered to boost regional connectivity and tourism; and
(d) the timelines and funding model proposed, if viable?

(a) whether Government has a plan to promote tourism in the Poonch-Rajouri districts, if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether there is any plan to develop the seven lakes in the Poonch and Rajouri hilly areas of Jammu & Kashmir (J&K), and if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether the Ministry has initiated a homestay programme for tourists in J&K, if so, the details thereof, district-wise; and
(d) whether Government has encouraged local community participation in sustainable tourism, and if so,  the details thereof, district-wise?

(a) whether under Forest Right Act (FRA), 2006, individual and community rights have been bestowed in J&K, if so, the details thereof, district-wise;
(b) whether any plantation drive has been conducted under CAMPA in J&K in last five years, if so, the details thereof, expenditure and species planted;
(c) whether Government has conducted any forest protection drive in last five years in J&K, if so, the details of expenditure, compartment-wise; and
(d) whether J&K Forest Department has provided any employment avenues to forest dwellers/tribals, if so, the details thereof?

(a) what impact the National Education Policy (NEP) has on the educational landscape of UT of Jammu and Kashmir;
(b) the key reforms introduced by Jammu and Kashmir Education Department, JK Board of School Education (BOSE), and JK State Council of Educational Research and Training (JKSCERT) since 2020;
(c) in what manner Annual Transfer Drive (ATD) policy has improved education sector in J&K;
(d) the total number of representations received for rationalization, whether similarly placed representations were rejected and if so, what criteria were used to make such determinations; and 
(e) whether kins of officers were given preference in adjustment in ATD?

(a) the current status of the newly established AIIMS and Government medical colleges (GMCs) in Jammu and Kashmir (J&K);
(b) the availability of trained staff to operate medical equipment in these AIIMS/GMCs;
(c) the number of MRI and CT Scan machines available in AIIMS/GMCs in J&K;
(d) the number of referral cases from District Hospitals and new GMCs to AIIMS/GMCH Jammu/Srinagar;
(e) the number of trauma centers between Batote and Doda in Jammu and Kashmir;
(f) the current staff position in J&K AIIMS/GMCs, whether there are any ongoing plans to address potential staff shortages in these medical institutions; and
(g) the status of Medi-cities in Jammu and Kashmir?

(a) the comprehensive update on the number of cases of land diversification processed under the Forest Rights Act (FRA) 2006 across India, specifying the progress made in each State;
(b) the details of copies of the pilot projects initiated under the FRA for land diversification, along with documented success stories, to offer insight into the effectiveness of these initiatives; and
(c) whether there is any predetermined time schedule for obtaining a clearance from the relevant agencies for land diversification projects under the FRA, if so, the details on established timelines and any measures taken to ensure timely approvals?

(a) whether Government provides list of current Members serving on the Airport Advisory Committee (AAC) in India;
(b) whether MPs from Rajya Sabha are included as members of the AAC, if not, the specific reasons for their exclusion;
(c) manner in which Government ensures that AAC represents a wide range of stakeholders & expertise;
(d) manner in which AACs collaborate with MPs of Rajya Sabha, to incorporate their insights and address aviation-related concerns; and
(e) the steps being taken to enhance transparency & accountability within the AAC, thereby ensuring that its decisions and recommendations align with the interests of public and aviation sector?

(a) how many Housing colonies have been established by Housing Department, JK Housing Board, Srinagar Development Authority, Jammu Development Authority for SCs, STs, OBCs, EWS, poor in J&K during last five years;
(b) how many commercial sites have been developed for SCs, STs, OBCs, EWS, tribals and poor in J&K and allotted to them;
(c) whether there is any proposal for setting up and allotting affordable housing units to tribals, SCs, STs, OBCs, EWS, poor in J&K; and
(d) which were the housing colonies set up by J&K Government, year-wise, during last five years and how many housing units were allotted to Tribals, SC, ST, OBC, EWS, poor?

rk

(a) how much funds have been sanctioned, year-wise during last five years, for preservation of Lakes in Jammu and Kashmir;
(b) funds spent for preservation of each Lake in Jammu and Kashmir and area-wise recovery of lake's area;
(c) how much funds have been utilized and how much remained unspent; 
(d) how much funds have been spent on Dal Lake and outcome of the funds spent in restoring the lake; and
(e) what are the proposals for Gharana wetland, Mansar, Sruinsar and other lakes in Jammu region?

rk

(a) the specific schemes promoting tourism in tribal dominated areas;
(b) the details of employment generated among tribal people by such schemes during the last five years;
(c) the number of proposals under PRASHAD Scheme received from Jammu and Kashmir and the status thereof;
(d) the reasons for Purmandal-Uttervahini development project under PRASHAD scheme still awaiting clearance;
(e) the budget allocated for development of tourism in Jammu, Doda, Kishtwar, Poonch and Rajouri districts and for Kashmir region, year-wise since 2018; and
(f) the status of schemes for pilgrimage tourism?

(a) whether there is any law for limiting the number of driving hours a for commercial drivers, if so, whether any technology is used so that commercial vehicle doesn't move after specified hours;
(b) number of accidents occurred in the hilly districts of Kishtwar, Doda, Ramban, Union Territory of Jammu & Kashmir and number lives lost;
(c) the preventive measures taken for avoiding such accidents;
(d) length of roads in U.T. of J&K provided with protective fencing/barriers especially in hilly districts; and
(e) the number of length of roads which has no protective barrier?

D

(a) the provisions available on National Highways, State Highways and district Roads for transhumance of animals by tribal communities and others in the country;
(b) if not, whether Government of India proposes to make a separate lane for transhumance of such animals; and
(c) number of deaths of humans and animals occurred during transhumance of animals during last five years, details thereof?
